  "validation_notes": [
    "Six distinct affected test groups pass on both platforms across recorded phases. Earlier failed window/layout iterations are superseded by the final accepted GUI tests, not counted as passes.",
    "Visual inspection exposed disappearing dropdown text when limits expanded. The layout now propagates a minimum content size and scrolls instead; tests require readable dropdown heights and access to the full work-limit control.",
    "The offscreen harness uses shown widgets and settles layout events without user input. Its scroll assertion checks the complete field at the end of the scroll range; Qt ensureWidgetVisible can follow a spin-box edit cursor rather than its entire frame.",
    "The test exits its event loop directly after success to avoid an unsaved-project close prompt from the shown offscreen window. No keyboard/mouse injection or OS screen capture was used.",
    "Catalog/project/GUI integration only in this round. No compiler geometry or inference algorithm changed; the previous inference/rebuild corpus remains separately documented.",
    "Raw report previews remain bounded to 5 MiB; the UI now makes that limit explicit and complete reports stay in the run folder.",
    "No proposal overlays, per-brush accept/reject controls or saved manual overrides yet. Original source grouping and light arrangements are not proven recovered. Portable 0.3.0 packaging is unchanged."
  ]
